SUMMARY:Deadline: SAT: Research-Creation Residency Program in Arts and Tech
 nologies 2026-28 (Montreal)
DESCRIPTION:The Societe des arts technologiques (SAT) in Montreal runs a re
 search-creation residency program in arts and technologies for artists and
  collectives working in the performing arts and/or media arts. The residen
 cy funds a research-creation stage of a project in technological arts rath
 er than the finalisation of a finished work\, so the call weighs the explo
 ration process and the innovation in it above a polished outcome. Each sel
 ected project receives a CAD 10\,000 grant\, whether the applicant is an i
 ndividual artist or a collective\, plus access to SAT spaces and equipment
 \, technical and creative support from the SAT teams\, mentoring and train
 ing activities\, and documentation and archiving. Access to spaces and equ
 ipment is assessed against the project's needs and granted subject to avai
 lability. Travel\, meal and accommodation costs beyond the grant are not c
 overed. Open to professional artists and artistic collectives worldwide\, 
 at any level of experience and from any primary discipline\, provided the 
 profile and project suit immersive technologies\; collectives must submit 
 a joint portfolio showing they can carry out the project independently\, p
 articularly the visual and sound creation inside a dome. Each application 
 must include a form and supporting documents setting out the concept\, the
  technical solutions considered\, and what will be explored during the res
 idency. One application per project and per person\; incomplete applicatio
 ns are not evaluated\; use permanent\, downloadable links rather than WeTr
 ansfer or similar temporary services. Accommodations and alternative suppo
 rt documents (large print and so on) are available on request at residence
 s@sat.qc.ca. Deadline 18 October 2026. Apply through the Google Form linke
 d from the SAT open-call page.\n\nOrganisation: Societe des arts technolog
 iques (SAT)\nLocation: Societe des arts technologiques\, 1201 Boulevard Sa
 int-Laurent\, Montreal\, QC\, Canada. Open to professional artists and col
 lectives from anywhere in the world\; no nationality restriction stated.\n
 Award: CAD 10\,000 grant per selected project\, for individual artists and
  collectives alike. Also included: access to SAT workspaces during the res
 idency periods\, access to equipment and software resources subject to ava
 ilability\, mentoring and training activities (on site and remote)\, creat
 ive and technical support from the SAT teams\, and documentation and archi
 ving of the work. Travel\, meals and accommodation beyond the grant are NO
 T covered. No application fee.\nDuration: Two months\, extendable up to th
 ree months depending on the project\; residencies run across the 2026-28 p
 rogram.\n\nMore: https://sat.qc.ca/en/calls/research-creation-residency-pr
 ogram-in-arts-technologies-2026-28?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://sat.qc.ca/en/calls/research-creation-residency-program-in-arts-
 technologies-2026-28?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refe
 rral
LOCATION:Societe des arts technologiques\, 1201 Boulevard Saint-Laurent\, M
 ontreal\, QC\, Canada. Open to professional artists and collectives from a
 nywhere in the world\; no nationality restriction stated.
